        idempotencyKey: str = ...,
    ) -> Result:
        """Auto Switch Multicam

        Cuts a multicam clip to whoever is speaking, on this computer: the active speaker's close-up after a minimum hold, cut a little before they start, the wide shot for crosstalk, laughter, long pauses and for variety on long monologues, optional reaction shots, never in the middle of a word. Presets: calm (podcast), interview, energetic; every rule tunable. The result is ordinary angle cuts (editable afterwards), one undo step, each with its reason ("Cut to Cam B: Speaker 2 starts talking"); dryRun previews them.

        Command ``multicam.autoSwitch`` (needs EditSequence; runs an AI model, so MediaAnalysis is needed too).
        Returns the Result of the edit (``.data`` holds the command's own answer).

        Args:
            _params: The parameters as one dict instead of keywords (a keyword wins); for a name that
                cannot be a keyword.
            angles: Your angle assignments; they win over the guesses.
            avoidMidWord: Move cuts to the nearest pause between words (default true).
            clip: The multicam clip (its picture or sound; default: the sequence's first).
            faces: Look at the cameras' faces (default true; false is quicker on long recordings).
            lead: Seconds a cut comes before the speaker starts (a J-cut).
            maxSnap: Seconds a cut may move to reach a pause.
            minHold: Seconds a shot is held at least.
            openLength: Seconds of that opening wide shot.
            openWide: Open on the wide shot.
            overlapMin: Seconds of crosstalk before going wide.
            preset: Podcast calm, Interview (default) or Energetic.
            reactionHold: Seconds a reaction shot lasts at least.
            reactionStrength: How strong a reaction must be (0..1).
            reactions: Cut to a listener's close-up when they react strongly (laughter, a quick word).
            sequence: Sequence id; only needed when the project has several.
            silenceWide: Seconds of silence before going wide (0 = never).
            target: Switch the picture only (default: the sound stays the mic mix) or both.
            varietyAfter: Seconds on one close-up before a short wide shot (0 = never).
            varietyLength: Seconds that variety wide shot lasts.
            wideOnLaughter: The wide shot for laughter.
            wideOnOverlap: The wide shot when people talk over each other.
            dryRun: Preview the edit without committing it.
            expectedRevision: Fail with StaleRevision unless the project is at this revision.
            idempotencyKey: A repeated call with the same key returns the first result.
        """

