    def transcribe(
        self,
        _params: dict[str, Any] | None = ...,
        /,
        *,
        check: bool = ...,
        clips: list[int | TranscriptTranscribe_ClipsItem] = ...,
        force: bool = ...,
        language: str = ...,
        media: list[int | str] = ...,
        mixedLanguages: bool = ...,
        provider: str = ...,
        sequence: int = ...,
        translate: bool = ...,
        vocabulary: list[str] = ...,
    ) -> Any:
        """Transcribe Media

        Transcribes the audio of media items or clips (default: every audio clip of the sequence) so the other transcript commands have words. provider: "auto" (on this computer when the local engine is built, else the user's cloud transcription model), "local", or "cloud:<model id>"; cloud transcription goes through the user's consent, spend cap and offline / no-cloud locks. Audio that already has a transcript is not transcribed again unless "force". "check": true only lists the providers and what has a transcript. Transcripts are stored per source file (the analysis cache), not in the project.

        Command ``transcript.transcribe`` (needs MediaAnalysis; runs an AI model, so MediaAnalysis is needed too).
        Returns the command's answer (the data of the read).

        Args:
            _params: The parameters as one dict instead of keywords (a keyword wins); for a name that
                cannot be a keyword.
            check: Only list providers, languages and which audio has a transcript. Default false. (Default: False.)
            clips: Clips whose media to transcribe.
            force: Transcribe even audio that has a transcript (the new one replaces the old: how to redo it in another language). Default false. (Default: False.)
            language: The language spoken: "auto" (default: detected) or an ISO 639-1 code such as "he", "id", "uk", "ar", "pl", "tr", "is", "fi", "cs", "sk", "ro", "hr", "sr", "bs" ("check": true lists all of them with their own names and how well Whisper knows them). Naming it helps a short or noisy recording that detection gets wrong.
            media: Media items to transcribe.
            mixedLanguages: The recording switches between languages (an interview with a translator, a streamer who changes language): with "language" "auto", every stretch of speech is transcribed in the language it is spoken in, and each transcript segment names its own (transcript.get shows them). Local transcription only, with a multilingual model (Small or larger tells languages apart best); slower, since the audio is listened to in short pieces. Ignored with a named language or "translate". Default false. (Default: False.)
            provider: "auto" (default), "local" or "cloud:<model id>".
            sequence: Sequence id; only needed when the project has several.
            translate: Whisper's translate task: the transcript comes out in English, whatever the language spoken (Icelandic or Finnish interviews, say). Local transcription only, with a multilingual model (Small, Medium or Large v3 translate best). Default false. (Default: False.)
            vocabulary: Words the recogniser should spell right (character names, game titles, jargon). Default: the project's custom words (transcript.setCustomWords). The local transcriber uses the first ones that fit its vocabulary hint (about 480 bytes), a cloud transcriber the first 100 as key terms. [] means none.
        """

